Date: 2022-08-25 What Is Claimed Is:
1. A method for providing operating data for an at least semi- automated vehicle, comprising the following steps:
sensorially detecting surroundings data using a surroundings sensor system of the vehicle;
conveying the sensorially detected surroundings data to a cloud, and conveying a request to the cloud for localization data;
receiving the localization data from the cloud;
ascertaining the operating data for use in a cooperative driving maneuver of the vehicle with at least one further road user using the localization data received from the cloud and the sensorially detected surroundings data; and
initiating the cooperative driving maneuver using the ascertained operating data.
2. The method as recited in claim 1, wherein the localization data received from the cloud include at least one of the following: distance of the vehicle up to a lane change zone, length of a lane change zone, a position of the vehicle.
3. The method as recited in claim 1, wherein the sensorially detected surroundings data of the vehicle are detected using at least one of the following: radar sensor, LIDAR sensor, ultrasonic sensor, camera.
4. The method as recited in claim 1, wherein the localization data received from the cloud are displayed in an electronic horizon of the vehicle.
5. The method as recited in claim 1, wherein the conveyance of a request to the cloud for data relating to cooperative driving of the vehicle is carried out when the vehicle enters into a defined mapping area of a digital map.
6. A device for providing operating data for an at least semi- automated vehicle, comprising:
a first interface for a wireless connection to a cloud for receiving localization data from the cloud;
a second interface for feeding sensorially detected surroundings data;
an ascertainment unit configured to ascertain the operating data relating to a cooperative driving maneuver for the vehicle using the received localization data and from the sensorially detected surroundings data; and
a third interface via which the operating data are output.
7. The device as recited in claim 6, wherein the device is configured to display the received localization data of the cloud using an electronic horizon.
8. The device as recited in claim 6, further comprising:
an electronic horizon, with which the localization data conveyed by the cloud is signaled.
9. A non-transitory machine-readable memory medium on which is stored a computer program for providing operating data for an at least semi-automated vehicle, the computer program, when executed by a computer, causing the computer to perform the following steps:
sensorially detecting surroundings data using a surroundings sensor system of the vehicle;
conveying the sensorially detected surroundings data to a cloud, and conveying a request to the cloud for localization data;
receiving the localization data from the cloud;
ascertaining the operating data for use in a cooperative driving maneuver of the vehicle with at least one further road user using the localization data received from the cloud and the sensorially detected surroundings data; and
initiating the cooperative driving maneuver using the ascertained operating data. 131818235.116 131818235.117 131818235.118
